---
import Layout from '../../layouts/default.astro';
---

<Layout title="Services | MECS" description="Practical IT services with clear fixed prices.">
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="hero">
      <h1>Our Services</h1>
      <p class="tagline">Practical IT help. Clear fixed prices.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Introductory section -->
    <section class="intro">
      <h2>Clear help. Agreed scope. Fixed price.</h2>
      <p>
        Each package provides a focused investigation, agreed safe actions where applicable,
        and a plain‑English summary of findings and next steps.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- General information -->
    <section class="general-info">
      <p>MECS provides remote-first support by appointment. Emergency, 24/7 and guaranteed-response support are not offered.</p>
      <p>The stated allowance covers the complete package, including the initial discussion, investigation, any agreed safe actions and the written summary.</p>
      <p>Prices shown are the total customer prices. MECS is not VAT registered, so no VAT is added.</p>
      <p>Where appropriate, additional remote time can be agreed in advance at £27.50 per 30 minutes. Larger, higher-risk or out-of-scope work requires a separate quotation.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Six service cards -->
    <section class="services-list">
      <!-- Windows or Linux Computer Health Check -->
      <article class="service-item">
        <h2>Windows or Linux Computer Health Check</h2>
        <p><strong>Price:</strong> £55 — up to 1 hour</p>
        <p><strong>Suitable for:</strong> Home users, sole traders, small businesses needing a general checkup.</p>
        <p><strong>Outcome:</strong> A plain-English summary of the checks completed, observed health indicators and recommended next steps.</p>
        <p><strong>Boundary:</strong> No repair or fix work is performed.</p>
        <details>
          <summary>See included checks</summary>
        <h3>Included checks</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>OS version and update status</li>
          <li>Antivirus/anti‑malware status</li>
          <li>Disk health (SMART status, free space)</li>
          <li>Memory usage and operating-system-reported memory errors</li>
          <li>Startup programs and services review</li>
        </ul>
        </details>

      </article>

      <!-- Linux Cleanup and Troubleshooting -->
      <article class="service-item">
        <h2>Linux Cleanup and Troubleshooting</h2>
        <p><strong>Price:</strong> £85 — up to 1.5 hours</p>
        <p><strong>Suitable for:</strong> Linux desktop or server users experiencing slow performance or service failures.</p>
        <p><strong>Outcome:</strong> A plain-English summary of findings, approved actions completed and recommended next steps.</p>
        <p><strong>Boundary:</strong> Cleanup actions require written customer approval. Logs, customer data and unknown or application files are excluded.</p>
        <details>
          <summary>See included checks</summary>
        <h3>Included checks</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>System logs (journalctl, /var/log) for errors</li>
          <li>Running processes and resource usage</li>
          <li>Disk usage and agreed cleanup of package caches and clearly identified temporary files</li>
          <li>Review of current firewall status, listening ports and user-account configuration</li>
        </ul>
        </details>

      </article>

      <!-- Docker Problem Diagnosis -->
      <article class="service-item">
        <h2>Docker Problem Diagnosis</h2>
        <p><strong>Price:</strong> £55 — up to 1 hour</p>
        <p><strong>Suitable for:</strong> Users running Docker containers facing startup, image, or daemon issues.</p>
        <p><strong>Outcome:</strong> A summary of the checks completed, evidence found, the likely cause where identifiable, and recommended next steps.</p>
        <p><strong>Boundary:</strong> Fixes are excluded unless a trivial reversible change is approved.</p>
        <details>
          <summary>See included checks</summary>
        <h3>Included checks</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Docker daemon logs (read‑only)</li>
          <li>Listing of containers, images, networks, volumes</li>
          <li>Inspection of specific problematic containers (no secrets)</li>
          <li>Attempt to reproduce the issue</li>
          <li>Docker configuration and version check</li>
        </ul>
        </details>

      </article>

      <!-- NAS, Storage and Backup Health Review -->
      <article class="service-item">
        <h2>NAS, Storage and Backup Health Review</h2>
        <p><strong>Price:</strong> £85 — up to 1.5 hours</p>
        <p><strong>Suitable for:</strong> Users of NAS devices, external storage, or backup solutions wanting a health check.</p>
        <p><strong>Outcome:</strong> A plain-English summary of the checks completed, observed storage and backup indicators, risks identified and recommended next steps.</p>
        <p><strong>Boundary:</strong> One NAS/storage system with up to four installed disks, or up to four external drives by agreement. No filesystem repair, RAID rebuild, scrub, firmware update, or test restoration.</p>
        <details>
          <summary>See included checks</summary>
        <h3>Included checks</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Storage system logs (if accessible, read‑only)</li>
          <li>Disk health (SMART status per disk)</li>
          <li>RAID or storage pool status and consistency</li>
          <li>Shared folders, permissions, and access controls</li>
          <li>Backup job configuration and last‑run status</li>
          <li>Backup destination accessibility and reported free space</li>
        </ul>
        </details>

      </article>

      <!-- Hardware and Performance Diagnosis -->
      <article class="service-item">
        <h2>Hardware and Performance Diagnosis</h2>
        <p><strong>Price:</strong> £55 — up to 1 hour</p>
        <p><strong>Suitable for:</strong> Users experiencing slow performance, crashes, or hardware‑related issues.</p>
        <p><strong>Outcome:</strong> A summary of the checks completed, likely causes where identifiable, and recommended testing or replacement options.</p>
        <p><strong>Boundary:</strong> No physical disassembly, hardware repair, or component replacement.</p>
        <details>
          <summary>See included checks</summary>
        <h3>Included checks</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>System logs for hardware errors (Event Viewer, dmesg, journalctl)</li>
          <li>CPU and temperature readings (if sensors available)</li>
          <li>Existing SMART health information</li>
          <li>Current resource and memory usage</li>
          <li>Device manager (Windows) or lspci/lsusb (Linux) for missing drivers</li>
          <li>A short, low-risk performance observation where appropriate</li>
        </ul>
        </details>

      </article>

      <!-- Home or Small-Office Network Diagnosis -->
      <article class="service-item">
        <h2>Home or Small-Office Network Diagnosis</h2>
        <p><strong>Price:</strong> £55 — up to 1 hour</p>
        <p><strong>Suitable for:</strong> Users with internet connectivity, Wi‑Fi, or device connectivity issues.</p>
        <p><strong>Outcome:</strong> A summary of the checks completed, likely causes where identifiable, and recommended connectivity or security improvements.</p>
        <p><strong>Boundary:</strong> No changes to WAN, LAN, DHCP, DNS, Wi‑Fi, firewall, or port‑forwarding unless a small reversible change is explicitly approved.</p>
        <details>
          <summary>See included checks</summary>
        <h3>Included checks</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Public IP address and internet connectivity from the router</li>
          <li>Router status lights and basic info (if accessible)</li>
          <li>Connectivity to the router (ping, DNS resolution)</li>
          <li>Wi‑Fi scan for channel overlap and signal strength (if wireless device available)</li>
          <li>IP address assignment (DHCP) and DNS settings on a test device</li>
          <li>Review of relevant WAN, LAN, DHCP, DNS, Wi‑Fi security and port‑forwarding configuration without recording credentials</li>
        </ul>
        </details>

      </article>
    </section>

    <!-- How it works -->
    <section class="how-it-works">
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Tell MECS what is happening.</li>
        <li>MECS checks suitability and confirms the scope.</li>
        <li>Attend the agreed remote session.</li>
        <li>Receive a summary and recommended next steps.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- Before we begin -->
    <section class="before-we-begin">
      <h2>Before we begin</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The customer remains present during remote access.</li>
        <li>The customer enters passwords themselves.</li>
        <li>MECS does not ask customers to send passwords.</li>
        <li>Important data should be backed up before approved changes.</li>
        <li>System-changing actions require your written approval.</li>
        <li>Remote access is removed or closed after the session.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Pricing boundaries -->
    <section class="pricing-boundaries">
      <h2>Pricing boundaries</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Payment buys the agreed time and work, not a guaranteed repair.</li>
        <li>Some faults cannot be fully diagnosed remotely.</li>
        <li>Work stops at the agreed boundary.</li>
        <li>Further work proceeds only with a separate agreement.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Call to action -->
    <section class="call-to-action">
      <p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="cta-button">Check whether your job is suitable</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>